  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Selecting fresh, quality seafood shows sophistication and culinary knowledge. Understanding what to look for prevents disappointing meals and demonstrates care in ingredient selection. For date night, serving excellent seafood creates a special, memorable experience that goes beyond typical home cooking."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "icon": "",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**In this guide:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "How to identify truly fresh seafood",
        "What questions to ask at the counter",
        "Storage and handling best practices",
        "Best seafood choices for impressing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Why Fresh Matters More with Seafood"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Seafood quality declines rapidly after harvest. Unlike beef that improves with aging, fish and shellfish are at their peak immediately and degrade quickly. The difference between day-old and week-old fish is dramatic."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Serving truly fresh seafood shows you understand this and prioritize quality. It's a level of care that translates to other areas."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/34ef5021-6dd2-4b31-9696-e9837b23f113/vudememe_A_hand-drawn_watercolor-style_illustration_of_a_select_af306609-f629-4a1d-9c8a-0b7198d52cda.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-80b2-9feb-c0a4f16d9584&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1775469600000&signature=Es1kZGSBQ7sgtHrM6swL3OD1bX2YhSRiNHEE1f4uJo8",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/how-to-choose-fresh-seafood-for-a-perfect-date-night.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Signs of Fresh Fish"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Whole Fish"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Eyes:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Clear, bright, slightly bulging (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Cloudy, sunken, or dull"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Smell:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Clean, ocean-like, mildly briny (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Fishy, ammonia-like, or sour"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Gills:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Bright red or pink, moist (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Brown, gray, or slimy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Flesh:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Firm, springs back when pressed (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Soft, leaves indentation, separating from bones"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Display:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Completely buried in ice, belly cavity filled with ice (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Sitting on top of ice, warm to touch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Fish Fillets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Appearance:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Translucent, glistening, vibrant color (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Dull, opaque, brown edges, gaps in flesh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Moisture:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Moist but not sitting in liquid (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Dry surface or pool of liquid in package"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Texture:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Firm, holds together, smooth surface (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Mushy, flaking apart, slimy feel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Smell:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Mild, fresh ocean scent (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Strong fishy smell, ammonia, sour"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Shellfish Freshness Indicators"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Live Shellfish (Clams, Mussels, Oysters)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Shells:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Tightly closed or close when tapped (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Open and don't close when handled"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Storage:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "In mesh bags, refrigerated, not submerged in water (fresh)",
        "Avoid: In sealed plastic, sitting in water, room temperature"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Weight:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Heavy for their size, full of water (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Light, hollow feeling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Harvest date:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Tagged with harvest date within 7-10 days (fresh)",
        "Avoid: No tag or old date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Shrimp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Color:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Translucent, gray-blue or pink (species dependent), uniform color (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Black spots (deterioration), yellowing, dull appearance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Texture:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Firm, intact shells if shell-on (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Soft, mushy, shells falling off"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Smell:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Mild, sweet, ocean-like (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Ammonia smell (means not fresh)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Frozen:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Most shrimp is previously frozen anyway",
        "Frozen at sea is often fresher than \"fresh\" thawed shrimp",
        "Look for individually quick frozen (IQF)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Scallops"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Appearance:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Ivory to pale pink, slightly translucent (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Bright white (chemically treated), sitting in milky liquid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Texture:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Firm, dry surface (fresh)",
        "Avoid: Mushy, overly wet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Dry vs. Wet:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "\"Dry\" scallops: untreated, better flavor (preferred)",
        "\"Wet\" scallops: treated with solution, won't sear properly (avoid)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ask specifically for dry scallops. They're worth the higher price."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Golden_Gate_Bridge_as_seen_from_Battery_East.jpg",
      "caption": "Replace with: Comparison of dry vs wet scallops showing color and moisture differences",
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/how-to-choose-fresh-seafood-for-a-perfect-date-night-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Questions to Ask at the Counter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Asking informed questions shows you know what you're doing and gets better service."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**\"What came in today?\"**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Fish counters receive deliveries on specific days. Today's delivery is freshest."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**\"Can I smell this?\"**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Any reputable counter will let you smell before buying. Fresh fish should smell clean."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**\"Is this dry or wet scallop?\"**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Shows you understand scallop processing. They'll respect the knowledge."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**\"Was this previously frozen?\"**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Not a dealbreaker (most fish is), but you should know so you don't refreeze it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**\"Where is this from?\"**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Local or domestic often means fresher supply chain. Also shows interest in sourcing."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Best Seafood Choices for Date Night"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Most Impressive"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Lobster tails**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Special occasion feel",
        "Easy to cook properly",
        "Pair with drawn butter and lemon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Oysters (if you both enjoy them)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Elegant, romantic, sophisticated",
        "Serve raw or grilled",
        "Natural aphrodisiac reputation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Whole fish (grilled or roasted)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Mediterranean vibes",
        "Impressive presentation",
        "Requires skill to cook"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Most Forgiving"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Shrimp**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Hard to mess up",
        "Cooks quickly",
        "Versatile preparations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Salmon**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Fatty fish, stays moist",
        "Widely liked",
        "Visually appealing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Scallops**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Quick-cooking",
        "Elegant presentation",
        "Rich, sweet flavor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Best Value"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mussels**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Inexpensive",
        "Look luxurious",
        "Easy to prepare",
        "Serve with crusty bread"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mackerel or Sardines**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Sustainable",
        "Flavorful",
        "Often overlooked",
        "Shows adventurous palate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Storage and Handling"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Immediate Storage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**At store:** Ask for extra ice to transport"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**At home:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Remove from original packaging",
        "Place on plate, cover with damp paper towel",
        "Set plate over bowl of ice in coldest part of fridge",
        "Use within 24 hours"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Before Cooking"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Remove from fridge 10-15 minutes before**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Seafood cooks quickly. You want slight chill, not ice cold."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Pat completely dry**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Moisture prevents proper searing and browning."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "What to Avoid"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**\"Fishy\" smell**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Fresh fish doesn't smell fishy. If it does, it's old."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Displayed on ice but not buried in it**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Proper display has fish completely covered with ice."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**No date or source information**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Quality markets provide harvest dates and sourcing details."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Seafood counter with no customers**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Slow turnover means older product."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Buying more than 24 hours ahead**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Seafood degrades quickly. Day-of purchase is ideal."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Market Timing Strategy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Best days to buy:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Thursday-Friday (weekend delivery)",
        "Day after delivery day (ask when they receive shipments)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Times to go:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Morning (freshest selection)",
        "Not Sunday evening (older stock)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Where to buy:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Dedicated fish markets (highest turnover)",
        "High-end grocery seafood counters",
        "Avoid pre-packaged in styrofoam when possible"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Date Night Advantage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Knowing how to select seafood shows several attractive qualities:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Attention to detail:** You notice subtle signs of quality"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Confidence:** You ask questions and make informed choices"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Care:** You prioritize quality ingredients for your guest"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Knowledge:** You understand food beyond following recipes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "When your date comments on how fresh the fish tastes, you can casually mention how you selected it. This demonstrates capability without bragging."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Is frozen seafood bad?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "No. Flash-frozen at sea is often fresher than \"fresh\" that's been sitting for days. IQF (individually quick frozen) is excellent quality."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: What's the white stuff that comes out of salmon?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Albumin (harmless protein). Appears when fish is overcooked or cooked too quickly. Brine the salmon first to minimize it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: How do I know if shellfish is alive?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tap the shell. Live ones close. Dead ones stay open and should be discarded."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Can I buy seafood the day before?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Yes, but quality declines. If you must, store properly over ice and use within 24 hours max."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Why does some fish cost so much more?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Seasonal availability, fishing method, sustainability, and supply chain. Wild-caught and day-boat fish command premium prices for good reason."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Quality Mindset"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Buying quality seafood is an investment in the meal's success. When you're willing to spend more for better ingredients, it shows you value quality experiences over just filling plates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This mindset translates to dating. You're creating a memorable experience, not just dinner."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "icon": "",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Quick Reference Checklist:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "ordered",
      "items": [
        "Visit fish counter morning of date night",
        "Ask what came in today",
        "Request to smell before buying",
        "Look for clear eyes (whole fish) or translucent flesh (fillets)",
        "Check for clean, ocean-like smell",
        "Store properly over ice at home",
        "Cook within 24 hours"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Fresh seafood makes the meal special."
    }
  ],
